<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.huffmanwrites.ollama-serve</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Applications/Ollama.app/Contents/Resources/ollama</string>
    <string>serve</string>
  </array>
  <!-- KeepAlive + RunAtLoad: this is a server, not a timer.
       Seven unattended jobs (the five report runners, wiki-check, repair-plan)
       reach their model through ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434, and
       before this job existed nothing guaranteed that server was running. The
       Ollama desktop app's own login item (2.com.electron.ollama) is DISABLED
       in the background-task manager, and its Squirrel updater helper only
       updates the app; neither starts the server. So the server ran only while
       the app happened to be open, and a reboot with the app closed left every
       AI job with nothing to call. The symptom is quiet: a connection error in
       a log and an article that never appears. wiki-check failed this way at
       13:30 on 2026-09-28, and the risk was recorded on the pending list from
       that day. This closes it: the server is now a launchd service, up at
       login and restarted if it ever dies.

       The binary is named by its bundle path rather than the
       /opt/homebrew/bin/ollama symlink, because that symlink is created and
       managed by the app and a dangling one would put launchd into a permanent
       KeepAlive restart loop. The bundle path cannot dangle while the app is
       installed, which is the only state in which this job can work anyway. -->
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/prh</string>
  <!-- OLLAMA_HOST binds IPv4 loopback only, deliberately. The desktop app's
       own server binds *:11434 on IPv6 (it is IPV6_V6ONLY), so this job's
       127.0.0.1:11434 coexists with it: the two sockets do not collide, and a
       `localhost` request resolves to this one. Measured 2026-10-07. Binding
       the same wildcard address the app uses is what would collide, so the
       narrow loopback bind is the point, not an accident.

       HOME is set so the server reads ~/.ollama (models and cloud auth) rather
       than launchd's default. PATH mirrors the other huffmanwrites jobs so any
       helper the server shells out to resolves the same way. -->
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>OLLAMA_HOST</key>
    <string>127.0.0.1:11434</string>
    <key>HOME</key>
    <string>/Users/prh</string>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/Users/prh/.local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
  </dict>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Library/Logs/ollama-serve.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Library/Logs/ollama-serve.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
